        </div>
        <div class="org-card">
          <h3>Naming</h3>
          <p>Name for what it is, not the process. <span class="mono" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--orange-600);">board-pitch-Q4-2026.md</span> tells future-you what this is. Not "final-v2-FINAL-actually-final."</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:var(--slate-500);max-width:700px;">Revisit your custom instructions too — now that you've actually used them for an hour, what would you change? Add "no jargon," switch to a formal tone, add date-stamping — whatever you noticed you needed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

